  "facts": [
    "The Pupin Bridge, opened on 18 December 2014, was financed 85% by China’s Exim Bank, marking China's first major infrastructure investment on the European continent.",
    "During construction, the bridge earned the nickname \"Chinese Bridge\" and even featured a controversial black marble slab that was later replaced after public protests.",
    "Designed as two independent structures, the Pupin Bridge spans 21.6 kilometres of access roads, diverting heavy traffic from Belgrade’s city centre while offering three 3.5‑metre lanes and pedestrian‑bicycle paths."
